    "question": {
      "text": "The iterative formula to find a root of the equation $f(x)=x^3-5x+7=0$ by Newton Raphson method is _______.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$x_{k+1}=\\dfrac{x_k^3+5x_k-7}{3x_k^2+5}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$x_{k+1}=\\dfrac{2x_k^3+5x_k}{3x_k^2+7}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$x_{k+1}=\\dfrac{2x_k^3-7}{3x_k^2-5}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$x_{k+1}=\\dfrac{x_k^3-5x_k}{3x_k^2+7}$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$x_{k+1}=\\dfrac{2x_k^3-7}{3x_k^2-5}$",
      "explanation": "Given, $f(x)=x^3-5x+7=0$\n$$\\Rightarrow f'(x)=3x^2-5.$$\nBy Newton Raphson’s method, the iterative formula to find a root is\n$$x_{k+1}=x_k-\\frac{f(x_k)}{f'(x_k)}\n=x_k-\\frac{x_k^3-5x_k+7}{3x_k^2-5}.$$\nTherefore,\n$$x_{k+1}=\\frac{2x_k^3-7}{3x_k^2-5}.$$\nChoice (C)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Engineering Mathematics",
      "topic": "Root finding methods",
      "subtopic": null,
      "tags": []
    },
