    "question": {
      "text": "Applying the secant method, the first approximation to the root of $f(x)=xe^x-2=0$, starting with function value at $x=0.5$ and $x=1$ is _______.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "1.1756"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "0.4035"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "0.8104"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "0.5473"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "0.8104",
      "explanation": "Here, $f(x)=xe^x-2=0$.\nBy the secant method, the approximate root after first iteration is\n$$x_2=\\frac{x_0f(x_1)-x_1f(x_0)}{f(x_1)-f(x_0)}.$$\nHere, $x_0=0.5$ and $x_1=1$.\n$$f(x_0)=f(0.5)=-1.1756,\\qquad f(x_1)=f(1)=0.7183.$$\nSubstituting,\n$$x_2=\\frac{(0.5)(0.7183)-(1)(-1.1756)}{0.7183-(-1.1756)}\n=0.8104.$$\nChoice (C)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
