    "question": {
      "text": "The extreme (minimum or maximum) point of a function $f(x)$ is to be determined by solving $\\frac{df(x)}{dx}=0$ using the Newton Raphson method. Let $f(x)=x^3-4x^2+5$ and $x_0=3$ be the initial guess of $x$. The value of $x$ after first iteration ($x_1$) is ______.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "2.70"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "4.33"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "3.30"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "1.77"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "A",
      "correctText": "2.70",
      "explanation": "Given, $f(x)=x^3-4x^2+5$.\n$$\\frac{df(x)}{dx}=0\\Rightarrow3x^2-8x=0.$$\nLet $g(x)=3x^2-8x=0$. Then\n$$g'(x)=6x-8.$$\nBy Newton Raphson method,\n$$x_1=x_0-\\frac{g(x_0)}{g'(x_0)}\n=3-\\frac{3(3)^2-8(3)}{6(3)-8}=2.7.$$\nChoice (A)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Engineering Mathematics",
