    "question": {
      "text": "In the process of evaluating $\\int_0^{\\pi/2}(x^3+\\sin 2x+5)\\,dx$ using Simpson’s Rule with $h=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$, the absolute value of the error does not exceed ______.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$0.12351\\times10^{-4}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$1.03503\\times10^{-4}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$3.01243\\times10^{-4}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$6.2475\\times10^{-4}$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "$1.03503\\times10^{-4}$",
      "explanation": "We have\n$$\\int_0^{\\pi/2}(x^3+\\sin2x+5)\\,dx.$$\nLet $y=f(x)=x^3+\\sin2x+5$.\nThe absolute value of the maximum error in Simpson’s Rule is\n$$|E|_{\\max}=\\frac{(b-a)h^4}{180}m,$$\nwhere $m=\\max\\{|y_0^{(iv)}|,|y_1^{(iv)}|,|y_2^{(iv)}|\\}$.\nHere,\n$$h=\\frac\\pi8,\\quad y^{(iv)}=16\\sin2x,\\quad a=0,\\quad b=\\frac\\pi2.$$\nThus $m=16$, and\n$$|E|_{\\max}=\\frac{(\\pi/2)(\\pi/8)^4}{180}\\times16\n=1.03503\\times10^{-4}.$$\nThe absolute value of the maximum error cannot exceed $1.03503\\times10^{-4}$.\nChoice (B)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
