          "label": "A",
          "text": "200 meters"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "210 meters"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "242 meters"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "262 meters"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null,
      "image": "images/Engineering_mathematics_6/gate-engineering-mathematics-test-5-q007-question-table.png"
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "242 meters",
      "explanation": "Given velocity at various times, the distance travelled in 12 seconds is\n$$\\int_0^{12}v\\,dt.$$\nBy trapezoidal rule,\n$$\\int_0^{12}v\\,dt\n=\\frac h2\\left[(v_0+v_6)+2(v_1+v_2+v_3+v_4+v_5)\\right].$$\nWith $h=2$,\n$$=\\frac22[(6+40)+2(10+16+20+22+30)]\n=242\\text{ meters}.$$\nChoice (C)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
