    "question": {
      "text": "A curve is drawn to pass through the points given by the following table.\n\nThe area bounded by the curve, the $x$–axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=4$, when calculated by the Simpson’s $\\frac38$th Rule is _____ square units.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "8.7562"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "5.7435"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "6.7134"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "8.4296"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null,
      "image": "images/Engineering_mathematics_6/gate-engineering-mathematics-test-5-q008-question-table.png"
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "A",
      "correctText": "8.7562",
      "explanation": "Let $y=f(x)$ be the curve that passes through the given points. The required area is\n$$\\int_1^4f(x)\\,dx.$$\nBy Simpson’s $\\frac38$th Rule,\n$$\\int_1^4f(x)\\,dx\n=\\frac{3h}{8}\\left[(y_0+y_6)+3(y_1+y_2+y_4+y_5)+2y_3\\right].$$\nWith $h=0.5$,\n$$=\\frac{3(0.5)}8[(1.0+2.9)+3(1.7+2.5+4.1+3.7)+2(3.4)]\n=8.7562.$$\nChoice (A)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
