      "correctOption": "A",
      "correctText": "3.1153",
      "explanation": "Given\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx}-xy=1,\\qquad y(0)=3,$$\nso\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx}=1+xy.$$\nAt $x_0=0$, $y_0=3$:\n$$y'_0=1,$$\n$$y''_0=x_0y'_0+y_0=3,$$\n$$y'''_0=x_0y''_0+2y'_0=2,$$\n$$y^{(iv)}_0=x_0y'''_0+3y''_0=9.$$\nUsing Taylor’s series,\n$$y_1=3+(0.1)(1)+\\frac{(0.1)^2}{2!}(3)+\\frac{(0.1)^3}{3!}(2)+\\frac{(0.1)^4}{4!}(9)+\\cdots=3.1153.$$\nChoice (A)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
