    "question": {
      "text": "The solution of the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx}=x+y$; $y(0)=0$ at $x=0.2$ by Runge Kutta method of fourth order with $h=0.2$ is ______.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "1.0034"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "0.0456"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "0.9984"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "0.0214"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "D",
      "correctText": "0.0214",
      "explanation": "Given\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx}=x+y,\\qquad y(0)=0,$$\nwith $x_0=0$, $y_0=0$, $h=0.2$.\nBy fourth-order Runge Kutta,\n$$k_1=hf(x_0,y_0)=0,$$\n$$k_2=hf\\left(x_0+\\frac h2,y_0+\\frac{k_1}2\\right)=0.02,$$\n$$k_3=0.022,$$\n$$k_4=hf(x_0+h,y_0+k_3)=0.0444.$$\nTherefore\n$$\\Delta y=\\frac16[k_1+2k_2+2k_3+k_4]=0.0214.$$\nHence $y_1=y_0+\\Delta y=0.0214$.\nChoice (D)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
