    "question": {
      "text": "In the process of fitting a quadratic equation of the form $y=a+bx+cx^2$ to a set of $n$ points $(x_1,y_1),(x_2,y_2),…..,(x_n,y_n)$ by the method of least squares, which of the following is not a normal equation?",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\sum y_i=na+b\\sum x_i+c\\sum x_i^2$"
