    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$\\sum x_i y_i^2=a\\sum x_i^2+b\\sum x_i^3+c\\sum x_i^4$",
      "explanation": "We have to fit\n$$y=a+bx+cx^2$$\nto the given set of points, with $a,b,c$ determined by making the sum of squared errors minimum. The normal equations are\n$$\\sum y_i=na+b\\sum x_i+c\\sum x_i^2,$$\n$$\\sum x_i y_i=a\\sum x_i+b\\sum x_i^2+c\\sum x_i^3,$$\nand\n$$\\sum x_i^2y_i=a\\sum x_i^2+b\\sum x_i^3+c\\sum x_i^4.$$\nTherefore the equation in option (C) is not a normal equation.\nChoice (C)",
      "status": "confirmed"
